{"parentUuid":"b3f17cb5-1d47-4e20-a869-0f616d969556","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"3aa9576d-6447-425b-bde5-2cc7b09b0a07","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"jiggly-crunching-zebra","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01TSPTcwPwa9gr34HS2BejBm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_011bXK2xYjnaeK4zCnMtfAza","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/pubchempy-name-to-smiles.md","content":"# PubChemPy: Chemical Name to SMILES Conversion\n\n## Overview\nPubChemPy is a Python wrapper for the PubChem PUG REST API. It enables programmatic lookup of chemical information, including converting chemical names to SMILES (Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry System) representations.\n\n## Installation\n```bash\npip install pubchempy\n```\n\n## Key Functions\n\n### Getting SMILES from Chemical Name\n```python\nimport pubchempy as pcp\n\ndef get_smiles_from_name(chemical_name: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Convert a chemical name to its canonical SMILES representation.\"\"\"\n    compounds = pcp.get_compounds(chemical_name, 'name')\n    if compounds:\n        return compounds[0].canonical_smiles\n    raise ValueError(f\"Could not find SMILES for: {chemical_name}\")\n```\n\n### Batch Lookup\n```python\ndef get_smiles_batch(names: list) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Convert multiple chemical names to SMILES.\"\"\"\n    result = {}\n    for name in names:\n        try:\n            compounds = pcp.get_compounds(name, 'name')\n            if compounds:\n                result[name] = compounds[0].canonical_smiles\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error for {name}: {e}\")\n    return result\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n- PubChemPy queries the PubChem REST API, so internet access is required.\n- `canonical_smiles` returns the canonical (standardized) SMILES string.\n- `isomeric_smiles` includes stereochemistry information (preferred when chirality matters).\n- The first result (`compounds[0]`) is typically the most relevant match.\n- Rate limiting may apply for large batch queries; add delays if needed.\n\n## Common Patterns\n```python\n# Single compound lookup\ncompound = pcp.get_compounds('aspirin', 'name')[0]\nprint(compound.canonical_smiles)    # CC(=O)Oc1ccccc1C(=O)O\nprint(compound.isomeric_smiles)     # CC(=O)Oc1ccccc1C(=O)O\nprint(compound.molecular_formula)   # C9H8O4\nprint(compound.molecular_weight)    # 180.16\n\n# Search by SMILES\ncompounds = pcp.get_compounds('CC(=O)O', 'smiles')\n\n# Search by CID\ncompound = pcp.Compound.from_cid(2244)  # Aspirin CID\n```\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":247,"cache_read_input_tokens":35828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":247,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtDZC7LGP89CHEo1Pjew","type":"assistant","uuid":"8032159a-c6ed-4648-87fd-8399e41066fe","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:14:53.798Z"}
{"parentUuid":"8032159a-c6ed-4648-87fd-8399e41066fe","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"3aa9576d-6447-425b-bde5-2cc7b09b0a07","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"jiggly-crunching-zebra","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01TSPTcwPwa9gr34HS2BejBm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01WKp1vSb7zoc1PiKHRuwbhh","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/rdkit-morgan-fingerprints.md","content":"# RDKit: Morgan Fingerprints and Tanimoto Similarity\n\n## Overview\nRDKit is a cheminformatics toolkit. Morgan fingerprints (also known as circular fingerprints, similar to ECFP) encode molecular substructure information. Tanimoto similarity (Jaccard index) measures the overlap between two fingerprints.\n\n## Installation\n```bash\npip install rdkit\n# or: conda install -c conda-forge rdkit\n```\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### Morgan Fingerprints\n- **Radius**: Controls the size of circular neighborhoods considered (radius=2 ~ ECFP4).\n- **nBits**: Number of bits in the fingerprint vector (default 2048).\n- **useChirality**: Whether to distinguish stereoisomers.\n\n### Tanimoto Similarity\n- Ranges from 0 (no similarity) to 1 (identical).\n- Formula: |A ∩ B| / |A ∪ B|\n\n## Code Examples\n\n### Generate Morgan Fingerprint from SMILES\n```python\nfrom rdkit import Chem\nfrom rdkit.Chem import AllChem, DataStructs\n\ndef smiles_to_morgan_fp(smiles: str, radius: int = 2, n_bits: int = 2048, use_chirality: bool = True):\n    \"\"\"Generate a Morgan fingerprint from a SMILES string.\"\"\"\n    mol = Chem.MolFromSmiles(smiles)\n    if mol is None:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid SMILES: {smiles}\")\n    return AllChem.GetMorganFingerprintAsBitVect(\n        mol, radius=radius, nBits=n_bits, useChirality=use_chirality\n    )\n```\n\n### Compute Tanimoto Similarity\n```python\ndef tanimoto_similarity(fp1, fp2) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Compute Tanimoto similarity between two fingerprints.\"\"\"\n    return DataStructs.TanimotoSimilarity(fp1, fp2)\n```\n\n### Full Pipeline: Name → SMILES → Fingerprint → Similarity\n```python\nfrom rdkit import Chem\nfrom rdkit.Chem import AllChem, DataStructs\n\ndef compute_similarity(smiles1: str, smiles2: str, radius: int = 2, use_chirality: bool = True) -> float:\n    mol1 = Chem.MolFromSmiles(smiles1)\n    mol2 = Chem.MolFromSmiles(smiles2)\n\n    fp1 = AllChem.GetMorganFingerprintAsBitVect(mol1, radius=radius, useChirality=use_chirality)\n    fp2 = AllChem.GetMorganFingerprintAsBitVect(mol2, radius=radius, useChirality=use_chirality)\n\n    return DataStructs.TanimotoSimilarity(fp1, fp2)\n```\n\n### Bulk Similarity Computation\n```python\nfrom rdkit import DataStructs\n\ndef bulk_tanimoto(target_fp, fingerprint_list):\n    \"\"\"Compute Tanimoto similarity of target against a list of fingerprints.\"\"\"\n    return DataStructs.BulkTanimotoSimilarity(target_fp, fingerprint_list)\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n- `Chem.MolFromSmiles()` returns `None` for invalid SMILES — always check.\n- `GetMorganFingerprintAsBitVect` returns a fixed-length bit vector (ExplicitBitVect).\n- `GetMorganFingerprint` returns a count-based fingerprint (UIntSparseIntVect) — use the BitVect version for Tanimoto.\n- `BulkTanimotoSimilarity` is significantly faster than computing individual similarities in a loop.\n- Radius 2 with chirality is equivalent to ECFP4 with stereochemistry awareness.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":247,"cache_read_input_tokens":35828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":247,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtDZC7LGP89CHEo1Pjew","type":"assistant","uuid":"6c7d8eb0-3529-4e67-ab0b-292ee54dcc46","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:15:07.366Z"}
{"parentUuid":"6c7d8eb0-3529-4e67-ab0b-292ee54dcc46","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"3aa9576d-6447-425b-bde5-2cc7b09b0a07","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"jiggly-crunching-zebra","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01TSPTcwPwa9gr34HS2BejBm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_017HR2P6oheWLkCFNRSeJbUz","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/pdf-text-extraction.md","content":"# PDF Text Extraction with pdfplumber\n\n## Overview\npdfplumber is a Python library for extracting text, tables, and metadata from PDF files. It provides precise control over text extraction and handles various PDF layouts.\n\n## Installation\n```bash\npip install pdfplumber\n```\n\n## Key Usage Patterns\n\n### Extract All Text from a PDF\n```python\nimport pdfplumber\n\ndef extract_text_from_pdf(filepath: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Extract all text content from a PDF file.\"\"\"\n    text = \"\"\n    with pdfplumber.open(filepath) as pdf:\n        for page in pdf.pages:\n            page_text = page.extract_text()\n            if page_text:\n                text += page_text + \"\\n\"\n    return text\n```\n\n### Extract Lines from a PDF\n```python\ndef extract_lines_from_pdf(filepath: str) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Extract individual lines of text from a PDF file.\"\"\"\n    lines = []\n    with pdfplumber.open(filepath) as pdf:\n        for page in pdf.pages:\n            page_text = page.extract_text()\n            if page_text:\n                for line in page_text.strip().split('\\n'):\n                    line = line.strip()\n                    if line:\n                        lines.append(line)\n    return lines\n```\n\n### Extract Tables\n```python\ndef extract_tables_from_pdf(filepath: str) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Extract tables from a PDF file.\"\"\"\n    all_tables = []\n    with pdfplumber.open(filepath) as pdf:\n        for page in pdf.pages:\n            tables = page.extract_tables()\n            all_tables.extend(tables)\n    return all_tables\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n- `extract_text()` returns `None` if the page has no extractable text.\n- For PDFs with simple lists (one item per line), splitting by newline works well.\n- pdfplumber handles multi-page PDFs automatically via `pdf.pages`.\n- Strip whitespace from extracted lines to handle formatting artifacts.\n- Alternative libraries: PyPDF2 (simpler), PyMuPDF/fitz (faster), camelot (table-focused).\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":247,"cache_read_input_tokens":35828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":247,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtDZC7LGP89CHEo1Pjew","type":"assistant","uuid":"2e2e7935-58a1-4186-87c9-770a7bb3f151","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:15:13.988Z"}
{"parentUuid":"2e2e7935-58a1-4186-87c9-770a7bb3f151","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"3aa9576d-6447-425b-bde5-2cc7b09b0a07","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"jiggly-crunching-zebra","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01TSPTcwPwa9gr34HS2BejBm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_018y42NSbcMHtz5sWt3PcxnM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/tanimoto-topk-sorting.md","content":"# Top-K Sorting with Tanimoto Similarity\n\n## Overview\nWhen finding the top-K most similar molecules, proper sorting is essential. Results should be sorted by descending similarity, with alphabetical ordering for ties.\n\n## Sorting Strategy\n\n### Python Sorting with Multiple Keys\n```python\n# Sort by similarity (descending), then by name (ascending) for ties\nresults = [(\"Aspirin\", 0.85), (\"Ibuprofen\", 0.92), (\"Naproxen\", 0.85)]\n\n# Method 1: Using sorted() with a tuple key\nsorted_results = sorted(results, key=lambda x: (-x[1], x[0]))\n# Result: [(\"Ibuprofen\", 0.92), (\"Aspirin\", 0.85), (\"Naproxen\", 0.85)]\n\n# Method 2: Extract top-k after sorting\ntop_k = sorted_results[:k]\n```\n\n### Complete Top-K Pipeline\n```python\ndef topk_similar(target_name, pool_names, pool_smiles, k):\n    \"\"\"Find top-k most similar molecules.\"\"\"\n    # 1. Compute target fingerprint\n    target_fp = get_fingerprint(target_smiles)\n\n    # 2. Compute similarities\n    similarities = []\n    for name, smiles in zip(pool_names, pool_smiles):\n        fp = get_fingerprint(smiles)\n        sim = tanimoto_similarity(target_fp, fp)\n        similarities.append((name, sim))\n\n    # 3. Sort: descending similarity, then alphabetical for ties\n    similarities.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[1], x[0]))\n\n    # 4. Return top-k names\n    return [name for name, sim in similarities[:k]]\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n- Negating the similarity value (`-x[1]`) converts ascending sort to descending.\n- Python's sort is stable, so the secondary key (alphabetical) is respected for equal primary keys.\n- When the target molecule appears in the pool, it will have similarity 1.0 — decide whether to include/exclude it based on requirements.\n- Alphabetical sorting should be case-sensitive by default (standard Python string comparison).\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":247,"cache_read_input_tokens":35828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":247,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtDZC7LGP89CHEo1Pjew","type":"assistant","uuid":"b8a60a63-2693-478a-8b26-444c904d1884","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:15:23.295Z"}
